  "title": "About Family Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "be5122a8320d633c",
      "text": "This plugin, type: **family**, gathers families of related wiki sites and adds them to your neighborhood. It augments the Present plugin: instead of only listing sister sites, you choose *which* families to gather."
    },
    {
      "type": "family",
      "id": "01b9d66d009aa2c7",
      "text": "FAMILY"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "625ddc4e896c6e27",
      "text": "Write one **command** per line (UPPERCASE, an optional trailing colon \u2014 see the [[Fedwiki DSL Skill]] convention):\n\n- `FAMILY` \u2014 `PARENT` and `SISTERS` together (shorthand)\n- `SISTERS` \u2014 sibling sites sharing the parent domain\n- `PARENT` \u2014 the parent-domain site itself\n- `CHILDREN` \u2014 direct sub-domains of this site\n- `DESCENDANTS` \u2014 all sub-domains, any depth\n- `FARM` \u2014 every wiki in the farm\n- `NEIGHBOURHOOD` \u2014 the sites currently in your neighborhood\n- `SNAPSHOT` \u2014 the current neighborhood *(same as NEIGHBOURHOOD)*\n\nAnd the **actions** (not site-kinds):\n\n- `ROSTER` \u2014 draw the gather compactly, mirroring a normal roster item\n- `TWIN` \u2014 only members that hold a page with **this page's slug**\n- `WATCH` \u2014 only members whose copy is *actually a fork* of it\n- `TITLE yes|no` \u2014 whether the `ROSTER` title shows (default yes)"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "7c1a4e0b9f2d5a86",
      "text": "### ROSTER, TWIN and WATCH \u2014 compact rosters of flags\n\nAll three render like a **roster item**: the members' flags flow inline in the grey box, each linking to that member's copy of the page, the (sub)domain on hover. `ROSTER` shows the whole gather (mirroring a normal roster, with an optional left-aligned title toggled by `TITLE yes|no`); `TWIN`/`WATCH` filter it:\n\n- **`TWIN`** is **existence-only** \u2014 a slug match in the member's sitemap, like the wiki-client *Twins* strip.\n- **`WATCH`** is **lineage-aware** \u2014 it fetches each twin's page JSON and keeps only those whose journal carries a `fork` event (`WATCH \u2286 TWIN`): who is watching your page.\n\nThe `ROSTER` and table views carry a subtle **\u2744 icon** that saves the gather as a roster ghost page titled after the commands (e.g. `PARENT SISTERS Rosters`). No separate `FREEZE` command.\n\n```\nSISTERS\nWATCH\n```"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "cedff82dadcf82fd",
      "text": "Each gathered site is registered as a neighbor, so its pages join your search and lineage. The page still reads normally without the plugin."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "c41e9b70a5d8362f",
      "text": "# Which Commands Cross\n\nA command language is a superset of an interface, never a mirror of one. Of the thirteen words below, five become a value of the `kinds` parameter and one is shorthand for two of those; the rest never leave the browser \u2014 `ROSTER` and `TITLE` because they are drawing choices the farm has no opinion about, and `NEIGHBOURHOOD`, `SNAPSHOT`, `TWIN` and `WATCH` because they read what only a browser holds. That last group is not a gap to be closed: no server could answer them however this plugin were written.\n\nThe table saying which is which lives in one module. The parser imports it and the plugin's interface declaration names it, so what an author may type and what the mounted operation accepts are one list read twice. See [[Family API]] for the rendered version, and [[About Farm Plugin]] for how a declaration becomes a route."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "47fd6339cb39a685",
      "text": "## Repositories\n\n- **GitHub**: [Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-family](https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-family)\n- **npm**: [wiki-plugin-family](https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-family) \u2014 `npm install wiki-plugin-family`"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "19d5c8a03e6b7412",
      "text": "# See\n\n[[Family API]] \u00b7 [[Farm API]] \u00b7 [[About Farm Plugin]] \u00b7 [[Fedwiki DSL Skill]]"
    }
